            "review_sentences": [
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_0",
                    "text": "The paper describes a question about discretize continuous features or group discrete features in the preprocessing step, which they call feature quantification.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_1",
                    "text": "It considers that a joint training of feature quantification and a discriminative model can lead to a better performance than treating feature quantification as a preprocessing step.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_2",
                    "text": "This paper has many typos, grammar mistakes and question marks, which make it hard to follow.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_3",
                    "text": "The question proposed is simple and easy to understand.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_4",
                    "text": "However, I don't convinced by the solution in this paper.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_5",
                    "text": "Since it is a hard optimization question, the authors proposed a relaxation approach in section 3.1.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_6",
                    "text": "I do not think that exp(a+bx) is able to approach step functions since exp(a+bx) is monotone.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_7",
                    "text": "I think Figure 1 is misleading.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_8",
                    "text": "For grouping discrete features, the author propose to use exp(\\alpha_{x_j, j}^h) and hoping that some \\alpha parameters can be optimized to be equal, which is too simple.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_9",
                    "text": "The exponential transformation here does not have an effect.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_10",
                    "text": "It is more interesting to consider how to add some constraints.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_11",
                    "text": "For example, if the discrete feature is ordinal, how one can assure that the grouped discrete feature is still ordinal.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_12",
                    "text": "The relaxation in this paper is too much without handling any interesting constraints and the proposed exp(a+bx) can not approach step functions.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_13",
                    "text": "The authors do not provide a good way to select number of cut points, which I think is a hard but interesting question.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                },
                {
                    "sentence_id": "human_rev_2_s_14",
                    "text": "The work also lacks value in literature review, optimization and experiments.",
                    "author_label": "HUMAN"
                }
            ]
